"notes": "Cash basis county; only a governmental activities column (no business-type funds). Receipts/disbursements come from the Statement of Activities (p2): program receipts (printed as totals, not by function line) plus general receipts; disbursements by function (printed as negatives, recorded positive). No single total receipts line is printed, so reported total receipts = 533,725 + 1,426,841 + 5,866,253 = 7,826,819 (computed). Beginning/ending cash = net position (cash and investments) beginning 6,225,445 (p2) / ending 6,182,841; investments of 322,246 are included in ending cash. Taxes 5,173,883 not split by type in the report (fund schedules show taxes only by fund; inheritance fund taxes 164,170), kept as taxes (unlabeled). Transfers net to zero between governmental funds (General out 497,780; Road in 400,000; nonmajor in 101,780 less out 4,000), so top-level transfers are null. Detail: General Fund, Road, Inheritance, Highway Bridge Buyback from budgetary comparison schedules (actual column, final budget); Highway Bridge Buyback and Inheritance disbursements are printed as '-' (none). The 11 nonmajor funds are recorded from the combining statement Total Nonmajor column (p12); the per-fund nonmajor budget schedules (pp7-9) are not recorded to avoid double counting. Cross-check: detail revenues 5,829,142 + 1,232,590 + 164,170 + 152,862 + 448,055 = 7,826,819 and disbursements 4,992,622 + 1,914,978 + 961,823 = 7,869,423 agree with the Statement of Activities. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
}
